{
  format: 1
  name: root-set-member-starts-empty
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#state-model", "§5.5", "§5.1", "#mutations", "§8.2"]
  note: '''
    The §8.2 ROOT half of `omitted-child-collections-start-empty`. §5.5: "When a
    containing row or struct is created, an omitted child set or keyed collection
    starts empty; an omitted non-optional map-valued field likewise starts as the
    empty map, never `none` — the set-analogous default, so the field's declared
    shape holds in every committed state." §8.2 says the root IS such a container at
    every moment: "The package root is durable state at every moment of an instance's
    life: the instance holds exactly one root whether or not any member has been
    written ... no written member yet is not an exemption." So a root `$set` and a
    root map-valued member that nothing has written hold the EMPTY container, not
    `none` — `none` is absence rather than a value (§5.1, A.1), and absence would mean
    the declared shape does not hold in a state §8.2 says the instance is always in.

    §5.5 gives the rule to "a containing row or struct" alike, so `cfg.labels` — a
    `$set` inside a root static struct whose sibling `name` IS seeded — is empty on
    the same reading.

    §5.1 is the companion: it exempts "a set or map-valued field" from the
    required-population rule for exactly this reason, so declaring `settings` without
    supplying it is admissible rather than an unpopulated required member.

    Wire (A.1/A.2): an empty set is `[]`, and a map is an array of `[key, value]`
    pairs, so an empty map is `[]` too. Neither is `$absent`.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.rootempty@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      flags: { $set: "text" }
      settings: "{ $key: text, $value: text }"
      cfg: {
        name: "text"
        labels: { $set: "text" }
      }
      $public: {
        readout: { $view: ". { flags, settings, labels: .cfg.labels }" }
      }
    }
    $data: { cfg: { name: "n" } }
  }

  steps: [
    { watch: "public.readout", id: "w0"
      expect_init: { value: { flags: [], settings: [], labels: [] } } }
  ]
}
